WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.200
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.850
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:12.980
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.250
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.780
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:28.290
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.160
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:37.320
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.140
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.090
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:48.620
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:52.530
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:56.550
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.970
Won't go away

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.790
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:07.930
We believed you

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:14.780
While we stand here

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:19.930
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:29.880
Zipang

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:40.870
Tomahawk... Missile away!

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.710
XO! The Mirai fired a Tomahawk!

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.510
You creep! Why you!

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.480
And you call yourself Japanese!?

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.900
If you want to sink our ship, why don't you do it yourselves?!

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.400
You could launch your own torpedoes at the Mirai,

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.110
but I think you are too afraid of its superior firepower...

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.320
So you're getting the Americans to do your dirty work?

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.410
What are you trying to pull here anyway?

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:25.410
To think that I made the mistake of placing my trust in you.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:30.000
I won't let you have your way with my ship!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.130
No matter what happens now, the missile...

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.460
...from the Mirai will definitely hit the American Carrier.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.170
But that sort of thing isn't what we are here for!

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.590
The Mirai's mission...

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.760
...isn't to take lives but save them!

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.810
But... because of you people,

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:46.930
the Mirai was forced to play her hand and...

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:49.440
...take this action to defend herself!

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.520
One minute to impact.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:13.130
Sinking The Wasp

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:33.860
There are fully armed torpedo bombers on deck...

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.090
Admiral! Are you alright?!

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.930
I'm fine...

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.760
Damage report immediately!

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:23.150
The engine room is flooded!

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.660
We've lost all power!

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:28.160
The flight deck and the ammo store are both on fire!

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.120
We can't get it under control!

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:34.170
We don't know how many casualties we've sustained.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:37.880
The flooding is getting worse!

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.750
The drainage pumps aren't working!

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.220
The ship is listing 11 degrees to starboard!

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.010
This ship is dead in the water.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.850
We have another 30 minutes at the most!

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:56.350
Admiral, we should move the flag to the San Francisco!

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.980
Separate the men into two groups.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.190
One will start to evacuate immediately,

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:06.820
and the other will do damage control to buy us some time.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.830
Recall the second attack force and...

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.200
...order them to take up an aerial perimeter to protect us.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.750
- Yes sir!
- Admiral, incoming message.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:16.250
It's from the target.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.670
We announce the conclusion of the battle.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.970
Our ship will now be leaving these waters.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:28.510
Many of your pilots are still alive and floating after...

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.180
...we shot down their planes.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.850
We hope you will rescue these men as soon as possible.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.020
Just one shot, and the Wasp is...

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.870
Is this the end?

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:01.670
All crew to abandon ship!

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.170
All crew, abandon ship!

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:07.510
Lower the boats! Those who can't make it, jump down!

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.930
Get the injured out first!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.640
- Yes sir!
- What about you, Lieutenant?

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:16.060
I'll go after I've confirmed everyone else is off!

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.140
Forget about me, attend to the Admiral!

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:20.560
Lieutenant!

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.730
Is that the same Sagittarius from Guadalcanal?

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.190
There's been rumors about an "arrow of god".

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.870
We are not living in a fantasy world!

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.410
We're in the middle of a war!

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:38.920
That's a new weapon! Nothing more, and nothing less!

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.170
It's a missile with a ground speed of 550 knots.

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:44.710
One of them destroyed an aircraft carrier.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.170
That's the whole truth to it!

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.300
Instead of obsessing over these silly stories,

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.510
you should be working to save my men, Ensign!

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.800
Now get to work immediately, double time!

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:55.430
Yes sir!

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.160
The Arrow of God...

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.160
That's impossible!

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.210
Then again...

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.170
Something doesn't make sense...

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.880
Neither us nor the Japanese have any weapons like this...

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:33.090
Lieutenant.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.470
What's on your mind?

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:39.020
- Nothing.
- I'll take full responsibility!

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.100
For now though, we need to get moving!

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.350
We must get off this ship as well. Hurry up!

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.880
Admiral.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.960
This was what I was thinking about just now on deck...

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.380
What if... that ship...

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:57.850
...really is supernatural... or something like that?

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:01.140
If it is an existence that is beyond mankind,

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.930
do you think we can still stand a chance?

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.980
An existence that is beyond humanity?

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:15.450
Annapolis didn't prepare us for a battle against that...

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:42.390
The Wasp... has sunk.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:12.380
Target Group Foxtrot is turning back.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.840
I think they're making a retreat.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:22.300
Our 250-mile surrounding perimeter is clear of land and air targets.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.270
Anti-aircraft teams stand down!

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.060
Recall the Umidori!

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:35.110
Anti-aircraft teams have stood down.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:38.530
Scan the surrounding waters and lower life preservers...

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.780
...if any American pilots are spotted.

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:49.420
I need to go freshen up.

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:51.420
Take over for 3 minutes. Look out for...

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.340
...any movements from the I-21 Sub.

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:04.850
Weapons Officer!

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:07.350
All hands, third shift!

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:09.350
All crew to switch over now!

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.320
Masayuki.

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:18.900
Yes?

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.700
Lieutenant, I'll take over now.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:22.360
Okay.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.090
Can you believe it?

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:46.220
A 15 thousand ton carrier...

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:49.390
Just 30 minutes...

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:52.940
It sunk in just 30 minutes...

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:57.570
And I was... the one who did it.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.650
I doubt they had enough time to fully evacuate.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.410
I wonder how many men...

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:07.740
...had to go down with the ship.

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.410
Hundreds? No, I'm sure there were more...

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:12.920
I feel so strange now.

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:16.460
This is exactly what I was afraid would happen...

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:20.920
...if I stayed in the SDF, remember?

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.930
I've killed hundreds with my own hands, and yet...

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.430
...it feels like I've just flicked a switch on a video game.

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:30.430
How is it that I can still stand here...

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:32.430
...feeling sane, like nothing has happened?

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:35.770
Tell me... what has happened?!

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:52.290
30 minutes since the Tomahawk hit.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:56.330
The carrier must have sank.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.340
Masayuki... I'm sorry!

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:01.300
When you're stuck at Military Command HQ for too long,

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.800
you forget what it is like...

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.760
...to be a soldier in a real battle.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.720
You have my thanks...

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:12.640
Mr... No, Lieutenant Commander.

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:14.600
Captain.

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:17.020
Do you think there's any ship that can...

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.360
...avoid a torpedo fired from this distance?

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:30.910
May I give you a word of warning, Mr. Navy Chief?

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:34.080
I don't want to rain on your parade.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.040
But forget about firing the torpedoes.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:39.340
It too late.

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:47.380
What do you think, Captain Shimamoto?

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.470
Can we hit the target?

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:56.640
This is bad.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:14:00.440
This sub is equipped with Type 95 carbon torpedoes.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:03.690
They have a speed of 49 knots and range of 8 miles.

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:06.400
If she fires all 6 tubes in a spread,

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.490
even the Mirai might...

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.700
What did the Commander say earlier on?

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.950
He said, it was too late?

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.450
What say you, seaman?

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.080
Yes. Well, that is...

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.750
- Yanagi.
- Sir.

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:22.540
How long has it been since we went under?

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:26.010
Um... I think it's been about 2 hours.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:32.850
You guys seem reluctant to tell Mr. Navy Chief, am I right?

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.810
Yanagi, explain to him why it's too late.

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:40.770
Um...

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:46.240
W-Well, the battery is dead.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:48.400
What's wrong with the battery?

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.120
The B-1 Type Submarine has a top speed of...

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:53.280
...up to 8 knots underwater,

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:55.910
and the batteries last for up to 1 and a half hours.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.620
It's been about two hours, since we went under.

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:01.920
You'd still need to engage the engines to chase down the Mirai.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.130
You see, that's why it's too late.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:08.970
You have to move into position first before firing the torpedoes.

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:11.220
Since the battery is dead,

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:14.430
you can only resurface and travel by diesel power.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:19.100
To resurface and then fire the torpedoes...

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:22.600
I'm sure you know the Mirai would detect you before you could fire.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.400
Let me tell you this, we may be on board this sub,

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.650
but the Mirai's Weapons Officer will not hesitate to take us out.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:33.530
2 lives versus 240.

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:38.000
He won't hesitate when it comes to protecting the Mirai!

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.670
What do you say, Captain?

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.460
Unfortunately, they are completely correct.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:51.050
The battery won't last more than another 10 minutes.

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:53.180
We can't follow them any further.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:02.390
What are your orders?

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.850
Prepare to surface!

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:45.520
CIC Sonar! Water discharge from I-21.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.690
215 degrees, distance 2000!

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:49.530
It's resurfacing!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:51.570
Prepare to engage!

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.990
Prepare to engage!

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:56.990
Ready to launch anti-sub torpedo.

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.580
Left, 215 degrees.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:01.250
Main guns, left, 215 degrees!

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:03.580
Alert the Umidori about the sub immediately!

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:36.820
Left 30 degrees, I-21 sighted!

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:50.040
Half speed ahead!

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:56.380
Incoming message from the Mirai.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:18:00.680
We are sending out a boat to pick up our crew.

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:03.810
Kikuchi, please aim well.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:06.890
I must say...

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:09.730
That Mirai... It's a superb ship...

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:17.200
I have another 30 minutes with you.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:19.910
Captain Shimamoto, is it true your battery...

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.490
...only had another 10 minutes of power left?

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:28.420
Well, as far as you know.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.000
Care to explain?

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:35.710
It intrigues me... That ship and her crew...

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:38.050
Especially her captain.

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:41.640
He actually turned back for the sake of two of his crew.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:44.140
He may have failed as a captain,

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.810
but he has my respect.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:49.390
I'd like very much to meet that man.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.810
Please let him know I said that.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:53.770
Yes.

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:01.070
Captain, incoming!

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:14.500
May I?

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:16.880
What is it?

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:18.800
It's a message for you.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:21.720
I know it's rude, but I took the liberty of reading it first.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:27.770
Terminate current mission...

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:30.140
...and return to base.

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:32.900
Lieutenant Commander Taki is to make a full report.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:34.980
From, Military Command.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:37.480
Someone out there knows my every move.

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:42.070
Thanks to your "mission", many have been hurt and killed.

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:44.950
If you had any shred of humanity left in you,

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.620
you'd know that.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:50.160
And now you have to bear full responsibility for your actions.

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:52.250
Don't run away now.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:54.250
I'm not the only one.

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.710
Even in Japan there will be...

00:19:57.710 --> 00:20:00.630
...those who're opposed to you and the Mirai.

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:04.470
Even Yokosuka will be a foreign land to you.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.430
Do you still want to go there?

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:10.480
I am...

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:12.640
...pursuing a certain soldier.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.770
Maybe you know something about him?

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:17.440
Former Combined Fleet Navy Lieutenant Commander,

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:19.440
Takumi Kusaka.

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:24.990
He's a madman who's trying to alter history for his own ends!

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:29.040
Kusaka...

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.160
Now I understand.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:34.120
I know him very well.

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:38.170
But he never possessed much foresight or courage!

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.710
He just follows orders!

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:41.670
I think you are the one who...

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:43.800
...gave him his "crazy" ideas, actually!

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:58.020
The restaurant's hotpot is outstanding.

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:03.860
When the water heats up, the catfish tries to...

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:06.820
...escape by tunneling into the tofu.

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:11.160
As they stew together, the soup's flavor is enhanced.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:14.750
The hotpot sure gives one a lot to think about.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:18.750
I wonder for how much longer we can enjoy such food...

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:22.010
Together with Admiral Yamamoto,

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:23.170
the Triple Axis in the Left Wing...

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:25.760
...of the Navy is against the war with the Americans.

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:31.260
You resisted the hard-line supporters in the navy.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:32.770
And now you say that...

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:35.350
...the mystery ship needs to be captured?

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:38.810
That's surprising.

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:44.030
Somehow... the catfish isn't going easily into the tofu.

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:49.780
Mr. Ishiwara,

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:51.830
a fish that's gone weak,

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:54.290
cannot even tunnel into a piece of tofu.

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:01.550
That ship called the Mirai...

00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:04.510
If we leave it alone,

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:08.260
it's going to present this country with some major problems.

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:17.370
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.530 --> 00:22:22.600
Just peacefully

00:22:22.100 --> 00:22:34.420
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.550 --> 00:22:47.300
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:53.940
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.500 --> 00:22:59.970
I kept on praying

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:11.820
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.690 --> 00:23:27.500
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.800 --> 00:23:42.890
There are still those in Japan who...

00:23:42.890 --> 00:23:44.680
...reject the existence of the Mirai.

00:23:44.680 --> 00:23:46.310
That was what he said to me.

00:23:46.310 --> 00:23:48.690
A port is crucial to a ship.

00:23:48.690 --> 00:23:50.190
Whatever awaits us at Yokosuka,

00:23:50.690 --> 00:23:52.730
we will find out when we get there.

00:23:52.730 --> 00:23:54.690
We've realized the ugly truth.

00:23:54.690 --> 00:23:56.940
To survive in this era,

00:23:56.940 --> 00:23:59.200
we cannot simply rely on righteous methods.

